    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, boasting the highest daily efficiency score at 65.74. Despite facing a formidable arm in Shane McClanahan, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a +16% park factor adjustment, keeping him in must-start territory. **Coby Mayo** also draws a strong 61.44 rating against the same starter; his ability to leverage the park environment while hitting in the middle of the order makes him a primary offensive engine for our squad. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** provides excellent value at 59.11, as his high-frequency stolen base profile\u2014a critical asset for our roster\u2014partially mitigates the concerns of facing a tough matchup, confirming his status as an elite hold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Heliot Ramos** (45.34). While he narrowly missed the starting cut, his projection was hampered by a difficult matchup against the elite stuff of Dylan Cease. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the upside of **Kyle Tucker** (58.24) and **Andy Pages** (52.83) to ensure higher offensive ceilings, even against tough competition. We must remain cautious with our utility and outfield slots, as every player today\u2014including **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Wade Meckler**\u2014is currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status. While favorable wind conditions in certain parks offer a slight boost to **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, the heavy reliance on pending lineups and matchups against high-end arms like Dylan Cease and Logan Henderson dictates a watchful approach to our daily game caps.",
